1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:02,540
Your phone rings. It sounds like someone

2
00:00:02,540 --> 00:00:04,960
you trust. They need money, right now.

3
00:00:04,960 --> 00:00:06,215
What would you do?

4
00:00:06,970 --> 00:00:09,850
Artificial intelligence can imitate a familiar

5
00:00:09,850 --> 00:00:13,010
voice. Sounding convincing does not prove who

6
00:00:13,010 --> 00:00:14,190
is calling.

7
00:00:14,953 --> 00:00:18,253
Scammers use urgency to rush a decision.

8
00:00:18,253 --> 00:00:20,153
A frightening story can make an ordinary

9
00:00:20,153 --> 00:00:23,198
request feel impossible to question.

10
00:00:23,953 --> 00:00:27,048
Before you act, make one independent check.

11
00:00:27,803 --> 00:00:29,923
Hang up. Call the person back on

12
00:00:29,923 --> 00:00:31,783
a number you already know. Do not

13
00:00:31,783 --> 00:00:34,973
use contact details from the suspicious message.

14
00:00:35,737 --> 00:00:38,957
Pause, verify, then decide. A familiar voice

15
00:00:38,957 --> 00:00:41,582
is a clue, not an identity check.

16
00:00:42,337 --> 00:00:45,057
Share this habit with your family. Agree

17
00:00:45,057 --> 00:00:46,757
on how you will verify an unexpected

18
00:00:46,757 --> 00:00:48,582
urgent request.

19
00:00:49,337 --> 00:00:51,437
If that call came tonight, would you

20
00:00:51,437 --> 00:00:54,182
trust the voice, or verify the person?
